# Look for objects on the table by an open-vocabulary prompt, view by view until found.

# What to look for, e.g. "red cube".
string prompt

# Views to try in order; empty uses the configured order. Each is an arm pose (an SRDF state) whose
# camera shows part of the work area: "full" all of it, "left", "middle" and "right" its thirds.
string[] views

# Instances scoring below this are left out; 0 uses the configured threshold.
float32 min_score
---
bool success
string message

# Valid only when success is true. Best first.
piper_msgs/DetectedObject[] objects

# The view they were found in.
string view

# Set on a failure: the views the arm reaches were looked at to the end and show none. False when a
# view failed (perception, motion) or none was reachable: nothing is known about the table then.
bool nothing_in_view
---
# The view being searched.
string view
